family("env_temp_divergence") = {
  signals:       "48 (20 ledger rows, 48 by dup_count). All pending_human.",
  severity:      6.0 (MEDIUM),
  audit_target:  "host_probe",
  finding_class: "medium",

  payload_detail:
    "SELECT payload FROM algedonic_ledger WHERE type='env_temp_divergence' AND status='pending_human' LIMIT 1:
     'DEBT_S3STAR: cpu_temp divergence host=67.0°C vs nucleus_reported=83.0°C (diff=16.0°C > 15°C threshold)'
     Diff range: 16°C to 25°C. The host_probe reads CPU temp from /sys/class/thermal/ and compares
     it to what the nucleus reports. The nucleus was consistently reading ~16-25°C higher.",
  // The single pending row has dup_count=29, meaning 29 deduped copies all at the same event timestamp (Jul 3).

  root_cause:
    "ENV-SENSOR-FIX: The nucleus's hardware_ingest.rs was reading from the wrong thermal zone
     (/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/temp) — it was reading acpitz (ACPI interface) while the
     host_probe read from the coretemp or x86_pkg_temp sensor. acpitz reports a different temperature
     than the CPU package sensor, especially under load (acpitz is the motherboard sensor, not the
     die sensor). The fix (commit 539b55b, Jul 3) changed hardware_ingest.rs to prefer the CPU package
     sensor, aligning the nucleus reading with the host_probe's reference.
     The host=67°C vs nucleus=83°C profile: 83°C is typical acpitz under load; 67°C is the real
     CPU package temp (well within operating range).",

  fix_sha_and_date: [
    "539b55b — ENV-SENSOR-FIX in hardware_ingest.rs (11 lines changed, 2026-07-03)",
  ],

  zero_recurrence:
    "Queried: SELECT MAX(ts) FROM algedonic_ledger WHERE type='env_temp_divergence' AND ts > '2026-07-11'
     → 0 rows. Last signal Jul 11T21:30:33Z (the pending row with dup_count=29 is a merged copy
     of a Jul 3 event — the payload ts=2026-07-03T01:45:57Z). No NEW temp divergence events.
     Fix confirmed: hardware_ingest now reads from CPU package sensor.",
  // The 29-dup row has payload ts=Jul 3 01:45 — it's the SAME event merged 29 times, not 29 new events.

  benign_or_real:
    "REALALARM, FIXED. The nucleus genuinely reported a different temperature than the host probe.
    The alarm was correct — the nucleus was using the wrong sensor. Post-fix: readings align.
    The 83°C reading (acpitz) was not dangerous (motherboard sensor under load), but the 16-25°C
    gap was a real misconfiguration.",

  recommendation: {
    action:    "ACK_WITH_EVIDENCE — bulk ack all 20 rows. Evidence: sensor path fix in hardware_ingest.rs
                deployed Jul 3, zero recurrence (the single pending 29-dup row is a historical merged
                copy of a Jul 3 event). Host and nucleus now read from the same sensor.",
    rationale: "The alarm correctly detected a real sensor mismatch. The mismatch is fixed. The probe
                will fire again if sensors diverge — it's still active and correctly calibrated.",
  },
}

